B.Ts=new A.t_("ROP","Test and consolidate your clinical understanding of ROP prevention, screening protocols, timing criteria, analgesia, zone/stage treatment, and post-discharge surveillance.","Multiple choice questions covering KPIs, prevention measures, screening arrangements, pre-exam fasting/preparation, gestational age eligibility, screening timing, zone treatment, and Stage 1 management.","Real-life bedside vignettes including oxygen titration, timely screening KPI calculations, transfer documentation, anti-VEGF surveillance, and aggressive ROP follow-up.","Retinopathy of Prematurity (ROP)","8 MCQs and 8 bedside clinical case scenarios based on ICMR / DHR STW guidelines.",B.ym,B.yw)
B.a57=s(["22+0 to 31+6 weeks","24+0 to 33+6 weeks","26+0 to 35+6 weeks","28+0 to 36+6 weeks"],t.s)
B.W5=new A.cn("ancs_mcq_1","According to the STW, antenatal corticosteroids are given to pregnant women at which gestational age (with a high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days)?",B.a57,1,'WHEN TO GIVE: "Pregnant women at 24+0 to 33+6 weeks of gestation with a high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days".',"When to give",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), WHEN TO GIVE')
B.a5H=s(["Dexamethasone sodium phosphate 6 mg IM every 12 hours x 4 doses","Dexamethasone sodium phosphate 12 mg IM every 24 hours x 4 doses","Dexamethasone sodium phosphate 6 mg IV every 6 hours x 2 doses","Dexamethasone sodium phosphate 6 mg orally once daily x 4 days"],t.s)
B.WB=new A.cn("ancs_mcq_2","Which regimen does the STW give under DRUG & DOSE?",B.a5H,0,'DRUG & DOSE: "DEXAMETHASONE SODIUM PHOSPHATE 6mg IM EVERY 12 HOURS X 4 DOSES".',"Drug & dose",null,u.aS)
B.a4W=s(["It is given as a single dose","It is effective, low-cost, widely available and more heat-stable","It is the only corticosteroid available in India","It does not need to be given intramuscularly"],t.s)
B.WH=new A.cn("ancs_mcq_3","Why does the STW prefer dexamethasone?",B.a4W,1,'DRUG & DOSE: "Dexamethasone is preferred: it is effective, low-cost, widely available and more heat-stable". The STW adds that the betamethasone regimen requires an acetate + phosphate preparation, which is not available in India.',"Drug & dose",null,u.aS)
B.a2L=s(["PPROM without clinical infection","Antepartum Hemorrhage","Severe pre-eclampsia/eclampsia","Multiple pregnancy alone"],t.s)
B.Wg=new A.cn("ancs_mcq_4","All of the following are listed in the STW as causes of a high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days EXCEPT:",B.a2L,3,"ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA 1 lists: spontaneous preterm labour, PPROM without clinical infection, Antepartum Hemorrhage, Severe pre-eclampsia/eclampsia, and planned preterm birth for maternal/fetal indication. Multiple pregnancy is not one of them; it appears under SPECIAL SITUATIONS as a reason NOT to withhold ACS when otherwise eligible.","Eligibility criteria",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA')
B.a1d=s([u.m,"Fetal growth restriction","Hypertensive disorders","Diabetes in pregnancy"],t.s)
B.Wi=new A.cn("ancs_mcq_5","Which of these is a reason NOT to give ACS according to the STW?",B.a1d,0,'WHEN NOT TO GIVE: "Clinical chorioamnionitis or systemic maternal infection". SPECIAL SITUATIONS: "When otherwise eligible, do not withhold ACS because of: multiple pregnancy, fetal growth restriction, hypertensive disorders, or diabetes in pregnancy".',"When not to give",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), WHEN NOT TO GIVE; SPECIAL SITUATIONS')
B.a19=s(["Repeat courses are given every week until 34 weeks","Two repeat courses may be given if needed","ONE repeat course only, if GA 24+0 to 33+6 weeks, high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days, and the previous course was started \u22657 days earlier","A repeat course is never given"],t.s)
B.Wa=new A.cn("ancs_mcq_6","What does the STW say about a repeat course of ACS?",B.a19,2,'WHEN TO GIVE REPEAT COURSE: "Give ONE repeat course only if ALL criteria are met": GA 24+0 to 33+6 weeks; high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days; the previous ACS course was started \u22657 days earlier. "Do NOT give more than one repeat course (More than one repeat course may cause fetal harm, and is not recommended)".',"Repeat course",null,u.eo)
B.a03=s(["Complete all 4 doses before referral","Give the first dose of ACS before referral, without delaying referral/transfer to complete the course","Give no ACS and refer immediately","Keep the woman until birth and refer the newborn"],t.s)
B.WF=new A.cn("ancs_mcq_7","What may a level I facility do for an eligible pregnant woman who needs referral?",B.a03,1,'REFERRAL/TRANSFER: "Level I facilities can give the first dose of ACS before referral, provided the pregnant woman meets the eligibility criteria, but referral/transfer should not be delayed to complete the course".',"Referral/transfer",null,u.dz)
B.a64=s(["\u226550%","\u226570%","\u226580%","\u226595%"],t.s)
B.Wl=new A.cn("ancs_mcq_8","What is the STW target for ACS coverage?",B.a64,2,"KEY PERFORMANCE INDICATORS: ACS coverage = women at 24+0\u201333+6 weeks identified with high likelihood of preterm birth who received \u22651 ACS dose \xd7 100 / all such women (Target: \u226580%). The target for appropriate ACS use is \u226595%.","KPIs",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), KEY PERFORMANCE INDICATORS (KPIs)')
B.a54=s([B.W5,B.WB,B.WH,B.Wg,B.Wi,B.Wa,B.WF,B.Wl],t.tw)
B.a1G=s(["Wait for labour to start before giving ACS","Give ACS: dexamethasone sodium phosphate 6 mg IM every 12 hours x 4 doses, starting promptly","Do not give ACS because of PPROM","Give ACS only if birth will be delayed until the full course is completed"],t.s)
B.Wv=new A.cn("ancs_case_1","What should be done as per the STW?",B.a1G,1,'All five ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA are met (24+0 to 33+6 weeks; PPROM without clinical infection; GA assessed accurately; no chorioamnionitis or systemic infection; adequate childbirth and preterm newborn care). "IMPORTANT: Start ACS promptly once eligibility criteria are met, even if the full course may not be completed before birth".',"Eligibility","A pregnant woman at 30+2 weeks (GA confirmed by early USG) has PPROM without clinical infection. There is no clinical chorioamnionitis or systemic infection. Your facility has adequate childbirth care and preterm newborn care including CPAP. She has not received ACS before.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA; DRUG & DOSE')
B.a04=s(["Give ACS routinely","Do NOT routinely use ACS at \u226534+0 weeks","Give a half dose","Give one dose and refer"],t.s)
B.Wf=new A.cn("ancs_case_2","What does the STW advise about ACS?",B.a04,1,'WHEN NOT TO GIVE: "Routine use at \u226534 weeks". DON\'Ts: "Do NOT routinely use ACS at \u226534+0 weeks or give more than one repeat course".',"When not to give","A pregnant woman at 35+1 weeks is in spontaneous preterm labour with regular contractions and cervical change.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), WHEN NOT TO GIVE; DONTs')
B.a4S=s(["Give ACS promptly","Give ACS after the first dose of antibiotics",u.eV,"Give a repeat course instead"],t.s)
B.W3=new A.cn("ancs_case_3","What does the STW advise about ACS?",B.a4S,2,'Criterion 3 ("No clinical chorioamnionitis or systemic maternal infection") is not met. WHEN NOT TO GIVE: "Clinical chorioamnionitis or systemic maternal infection". DON\'Ts: "Do NOT give ACS in clinical chorioamnionitis or systemic maternal infection".',"When not to give","A pregnant woman at 28+4 weeks with spontaneous preterm labour has been diagnosed with clinical chorioamnionitis.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA; WHEN NOT TO GIVE')
B.a6K=s(["Give ONE repeat course","No further ACS can ever be given","Give two repeat courses 7 days apart","Wait until 34 weeks"],t.s)
B.Wb=new A.cn("ancs_case_4","What should be done as per the STW?",B.a6K,0,'WHEN TO GIVE REPEAT COURSE: ONE repeat course if ALL are met: GA 24+0 to 33+6 weeks; high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days; the previous ACS course was started \u22657 days earlier. "Do NOT give more than one repeat course".',"Repeat course","A pregnant woman at 31+0 weeks received one ACS course that was started 10 days ago. She now has antepartum hemorrhage with a high likelihood of preterm birth within the next 7 days. She meets the other eligibility criteria and has not had a repeat course.",u.eo)
B.a2M=s(["Complete the full ACS course before referral","Give the first dose of ACS and refer for in-utero transfer to a facility with at least level II care (CPAP), without delaying referral to complete the course","Refer without giving ACS","Keep her at the level I facility until birth"],t.s)
B.Wh=new A.cn("ancs_case_5","What does the STW advise?",B.a2M,1,'REFERRAL/TRANSFER: "Pregnant women with likelihood of early preterm birth should be referred to a facility (in-utero transfer) with at least level II care (CPAP) for preterm infants"; "Level I facilities can give the first dose of ACS before referral, provided the pregnant woman meets the eligibility criteria, but referral/transfer should not be delayed to complete the course".',"Referral/transfer","At a level I facility without CPAP, a pregnant woman at 29+3 weeks with severe pre-eclampsia meets the ACS eligibility criteria (preterm newborn care including CPAP is ensured at the receiving facility).",u.dz)
B.a5l=s(["Withhold ACS because of twins","Withhold ACS because of diabetes","Give ACS; do not withhold because of multiple pregnancy or diabetes; monitor and optimize maternal glucose control","Give half the dose because of diabetes"],t.s)
B.W0=new A.cn("ancs_case_6","What does the STW advise?",B.a5l,2,'SPECIAL SITUATIONS: "When otherwise eligible, do not withhold ACS because of: multiple pregnancy, fetal growth restriction, hypertensive disorders, or diabetes in pregnancy"; "In diabetes: monitor and optimize maternal glucose control". DOs: "Monitor maternal glucose closely in women with diabetes".',"Special situations","A woman with a twin pregnancy and diabetes in pregnancy is at 32+1 weeks in spontaneous preterm labour and meets all ACS eligibility criteria.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth" (August 2026), SPECIAL SITUATIONS; DOs')
B.a2o=s([B.Wv,B.Wf,B.W3,B.Wb,B.Wh,B.W0],t.tw)
B.Tr=new A.t_("ANCS","Test your understanding of the ANCS STW: when to give, eligibility, drug & dose, when not to give, repeat course, referral and KPIs.","Multiple choice questions on the gestation window, drug & dose, causes of high likelihood of preterm birth, when not to give, special situations, repeat course, referral and KPIs.","Bedside vignettes applying the STW eligibility criteria, WHEN NOT TO GIVE, repeat course, special situations and referral/transfer boxes.","Antenatal Corticosteroids for Preterm Birth (ANCS)","8 MCQs and 6 clinical case scenarios written only from the ICMR / DHR ANCS STW.",B.a54,B.a2o)
B.a30=s(["BLOOD GLUCOSE <36 mg/dL","BLOOD GLUCOSE <40 mg/dL","BLOOD GLUCOSE <45 mg/dL","BLOOD GLUCOSE <60 mg/dL"],t.s)
B.Wz=new A.cn("hypo_mcq_1","Which blood glucose value is the entry point of the STW management flowchart?",B.a30,2,'The flowchart starts at "BLOOD GLUCOSE <45 mg/dL". HOW TO MONITOR: "Low value (<45 mg/dL): send a blood sample to the lab"; "DO NOT delay treatment for lab confirmation".',"Threshold",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Neonatal Hypoglycemia" (August 2026), flowchart; HOW TO MONITOR BLOOD GLUCOSE (BG)')
B.a5V=s(["Healthy term AGA neonate","Preterm infant (<37 weeks' gestation)","Infant of a diabetic mother","Neonate born to a mother receiving beta-blockers"],t.s)
B.Wy=new A.cn("hypo_mcq_2","In which of these neonates is routine blood glucose monitoring NOT required according to the STW?",B.a5V,0,'WHOM TO SCREEN FOR HYPOGLYCEMIA lists preterm, low-birth-weight, SGA, LGA, infants of diabetic mothers, neonates of mothers on beta-blockers, sick neonates and neonates following exchange transfusion. "Routine blood glucose monitoring is not required in healthy term AGA neonates".',"Whom to screen",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Neonatal Hypoglycemia" (August 2026), WHOM TO SCREEN FOR HYPOGLYCEMIA')
B.a3y=s(["1, 2, 6, 12, 24, 48, 72 hours","Every 2 hours for 48 hours","1, 3, 6, 12 and 24 hours only","Once daily for 3 days"],t.s)
B.Wo=new A.cn("hypo_mcq_3","What is the STW schedule of blood glucose monitoring for at-risk infants?",B.a3y,0,'SCHEDULE OF BLOOD GLUCOSE MONITORING: at-risk infants "1, 2, 6, 12, 24, 48, 72 hours" ("*in IDM, monitoring can be stopped between 24-36 hours provided feeding is established"); infants on IV fluids "Every 6-8 hours"; "BG should be measured pre-feeding".',"Monitoring schedule",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Neonatal Hypoglycemia" (August 2026), SCHEDULE OF BLOOD GLUCOSE MONITORING')
B.a1A=s(["2 ml/kg of 10% dextrose slowly over 1 minute","5 ml/kg of 10% dextrose over 10 minutes","2 ml/kg of 25% dextrose as a rapid push","10 ml/kg of normal saline"],t.s)
B.W9=new A.cn("hypo_mcq_4","What IV bolus does the STW give for a symptomatic neonate or BG < 25 mg/dL?",B.a1A,0,'SYMPTOMATIC OR BG < 25 mg/dL: "IV bolus: 2 ml/kg of 10% of dextrose slowly over 1 minute".',"Symptomatic or BG <25 mg/dL",null,u.d)
B.a68=s(["4 mg/kg/min","6 mg/kg/min","8 mg/kg/min","12 mg/kg/min"],t.s)
B.Wn=new A.cn("hypo_mcq_5","At what glucose infusion rate (GIR) does the STW start the IV dextrose infusion after the bolus?",B.a68,1,'SYMPTOMATIC OR BG < 25 mg/dL: "Start IV infusion of dextrose at a glucose infusion rate (GIR) of 6 mg/kg/min".',"Symptomatic or BG <25 mg/dL",null,u.d)
B.a1l=s(["Increase by 1 mg/kg/min, maximum 10 mg/kg/min","Increase by 2 mg/kg/min, maximum 12 mg/kg/min","Increase by 4 mg/kg/min, maximum 16 mg/kg/min","Double the GIR each hour"],t.s)
B.W2=new A.cn("hypo_mcq_6","On IV glucose, if BG remains < 45 mg/dL, how does the STW change the GIR?",B.a1l,1,'Flowchart: BG < 45 mg/dL \u2192 "Increase GIR by 2 mg/ kg/min (maximum 12 mg/kg/min)".',"Increasing GIR",null,u.g0)
B.a0t=s([u.cG,"Hydrocortisone: 10 mg/kg/day IV once daily","Dexamethasone 6 mg IM every 12 hours","Oral dextrose solution"],t.s)
B.W1=new A.cn("hypo_mcq_7","Which drug does the STW list for refractory hypoglycemia?",B.a0t,0,'DRUGS FOR REFRACTORY HYPOGLYCEMIA: "Hydrocortisone: 5 mg/kg/day IV in two divided doses"; "Additional drugs should be administered at a tertiary care hospital with workup for underlying causes".',"Refractory hypoglycemia",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Neonatal Hypoglycemia" (August 2026), DRUGS FOR REFRACTORY HYPOGLYCEMIA')
B.a4k=s(["> 5% dextrose","> 10% dextrose","> 12.5-15% dextrose","No limit is stated"],t.s)
B.Ws=new A.cn("hypo_mcq_8","Which dextrose concentration does the STW say to avoid through a peripheral vein?",B.a4k,2,'PRACTICAL POINTS: "Avoid > 12.5-15% dextrose infusion through a peripheral vein".',"Practical points",null,'ICMR/DHR STW "Neonatal Hypoglycemia" (August 2026), PRACTICAL POINTS')
B.a2J=s([B.Wz,B.Wy,B.Wo,B.W9,B.Wn,B.W2,B.W1,B.Ws],t.tw)
B.a58=s(["IV bolus 2 ml/kg of 10% dextrose","Immediate supervised feeding (breastfeeding or a measured volume of expressed breastmilk by paladai or gavage) and re-check BG after 1 hour","Wait for the lab result before any treatment","Feed a dextrose solution instead of breastmilk"],t.s)
B.Wp=new A.cn("hypo_case_1","What is the next step as per the STW?",B.a58,1,'ASYMPTOMATIC & BG \u226525 mg/dL: "Immediate supervised feeding"; "Breastfeeding or a measured volume of expressed breastmilk (Formula milk if EBM not available) by paladai or gavage"; "RE-CHECK BG AFTER 1 HOUR". DON\'Ts: "Do NOT substitute dextrose solutions for breastmilk".',"Asymptomatic & BG \u226525 mg/dL","A preterm neonate (an at-risk infant) has a point-of-care BG of 32 mg/dL at 2 hours of life. On examination there are none of the listed symptoms or signs.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Neonatal Hypoglycemia" (August 2026), ASYMPTOMATIC & BG \u226525 mg/dL')
B.a6b=s(["Supervised feeding and re-check after 1 hour","IV bolus 2 ml/kg of 10% dextrose slowly over 1 minute and start IV dextrose infusion at GIR 6 mg/kg/min","Re-check BG at 6 hours","Give hydrocortisone"],t.s)
B.Wd=new A.cn("hypo_case_2","What does the STW advise?",B.a6b,1,'BG < 25 mg/dL takes the "SYMPTOMATIC OR BG < 25 mg/dL" branch even without symptoms: "IV bolus: 2 ml/kg of 10% of dextrose slowly over 1 minute"; "Start IV infusion of dextrose at a glucose infusion rate (GIR) of 6 mg/kg/min".',"Symptomatic or BG <25 mg/dL","An infant of a diabetic mother has a BG of 20 mg/dL. The baby has no listed symptoms or signs.",u.d)
B.a15=s(["Continue feeds and re-check in 6 hours","Start IV glucose infusion","Stop monitoring","Refer to a higher centre for endocrine work-up"],t.s)
B.WG=new A.cn("hypo_case_3","What does the STW advise now?",B.a15,1,'RE-CHECK BG AFTER 1 HOUR: "Start IV glucose infusion if: BG < 45 mg/dL OR Symptoms develop". Then "Re-check BG every 30 min until 2 consecutive values are \u226545 mg/dL, then every 6 h".',"Re-check after 1 hour","An asymptomatic neonate with BG 34 mg/dL was given supervised feeding. At the 1-hour re-check the BG is 38 mg/dL.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Neonatal Hypoglycemia" (August 2026), RE-CHECK BG AFTER 1 HOUR')
B.a3q=s(["Increase GIR by 2 mg/kg/min to 10 mg/kg/min","Increase GIR to 16 mg/kg/min","Reduce GIR by 2 mg/kg/min","Stop IV fluids"],t.s)
B.Wq=new A.cn("hypo_case_4","What does the STW advise?",B.a3q,0,'Flowchart: BG < 45 mg/dL \u2192 "Increase GIR by 2 mg/ kg/min (maximum 12 mg/kg/min)"; 8 + 2 = 10 mg/kg/min.',"Increasing GIR","A neonate on IV dextrose at GIR 8 mg/kg/min has a re-check BG of 40 mg/dL.",u.g0)
B.a6f=s(["Increase GIR to 6 mg/kg/min","Stop IV fluids","Continue IV fluids for another 24 hours at GIR 4 mg/kg/min","Give a dextrose bolus before stopping"],t.s)
B.WE=new A.cn("hypo_case_5","What does the STW advise?",B.a6f,1,'Flowchart: "Stop IV fluids when euglycemic on GIR 4 mg/ kg/min and tolerating adequate enteral feeds". Before that: "Reduce GIR by 2 mg/ kg/min every 6 hours; Increase oral feeds; Monitor BG every 6 hours".',"Stopping IV fluids","A neonate who has been euglycemic for 24 hours on IV fluids has been weaned and is now euglycemic on GIR 4 mg/kg/min, tolerating adequate enteral feeds.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Neonatal Hypoglycemia" (August 2026), flowchart (stop IV fluids)')
B.a46=s(["Keep increasing GIR beyond 12 mg/kg/min","Consider ENDOCRINE/METABOLIC disorders & REFER to higher centre; drugs for refractory hypoglycemia include hydrocortisone 5 mg/kg/day IV in two divided doses","Start antibiotics for hypoglycemia","Stop IV fluids and feed dextrose solution"],t.s)
B.W8=new A.cn("hypo_case_6","What does the STW advise?",B.a46,1,'Flowchart: "Persistent (GIR requirement >3-7 days) or Refractory (GIR > 10-12 mg/kg/min for 24 hours) hypoglycemia" \u2192 "Consider ENDOCRINE/ METABOLIC disorders & REFER to higher centre". DRUGS FOR REFRACTORY HYPOGLYCEMIA: "Hydrocortisone: 5 mg/kg/day IV in two divided doses". DON\'Ts: "Do NOT give antibiotics for hypoglycemia unless sepsis is suspected".',"Refractory hypoglycemia","A neonate has needed a GIR > 10-12 mg/kg/min for 24 hours and BG remains < 45 mg/dL.",'ICMR/DHR STW "Neonatal Hypoglycemia" (August 2026), flowchart (persistent/refractory); DRUGS FOR REFRACTORY HYPOGLYCEMIA')
B.a2s=s([B.Wp,B.Wd,B.WG,B.Wq,B.WE,B.W8],t.tw)
B.Tq=new A.t_("Hypoglycemia","Test your understanding of the Neonatal Hypoglycemia STW: whom to screen, monitoring schedule, the management flowchart, practical points and refractory hypoglycemia.","Multiple choice questions on the BG threshold, whom to screen, monitoring schedule, IV bolus, GIR, peripheral dextrose limit and drugs for refractory hypoglycemia.","Bedside vignettes following the flowchart: supervised feeding, IV bolus and GIR, the 1-hour re-check, increasing GIR, stopping IV fluids and referral.","Neonatal Hypoglycemia","8 MCQs and 6 clinical case scenarios written only from the ICMR / DHR Neonatal Hypoglycemia STW.",B.a2J,B.a2s)
B.dg=new A.dn([B.at,B.Ts,B.aZ,B.Tr,B.an,B.Tq],A.ac("dn<cy,t_>"))
